tools.description:
Read/write the per-run asset library. The library is the catalog of every video clip in this run (auto-populated by download_video and clip_video) plus folders/tags/notes you assign. Returns are JSON-shaped {"ok": ..., ...}. To ADD media to the library, use import_media (a url, base64 bytes, or a local file/directory path), which returns a media_ref.

Pass exactly one `action` per call:

  * list          (folder?, recursive?) -> {clips: [...]}
  * get           (id) -> {clip: {...}}
  * update        (id, filename?, folder?, tags?, notes?) -> {clip: {...}}
  * move          (id, folder) -> {clip: {...}}
  * delete        (id) -> {removed_clips, ...}   # CASCADE: also removes every clip using it, across the timeline, as ONE undo entry
  * create_folder (folder) -> {folders: [...]}
  * rename_folder (old, new) -> {clips_moved, ...}
  * delete_folder (folder, force?) -> {removed_clip_ids, ...}
  * rescan        () -> {added, removed_catalog_rows, removed_dup_files}
  * resolve       (id_or_path) -> {path}

Folders are slash-separated path strings ("a/b/c"). They are pure metadata - no real directories are created. delete refuses by default if the clip is referenced by timeline.json (pass force=true to override).
